I'm Melissa Odin I'm the founder and CEO  of the abortion survivors Network  we are a healing and advocacy  organization that serves abortion  survivors so the babies who survive  failed abortions we serve survivors  around the world and their families  including their moms who are impacted  after an abortion fails and of course I  have my own backstory that led me to  creating this organization I myself am  an abortion Survivor in 1977 I survived  a saline infusion abortion that was  forced upon my birth mother by her  family I soaked in a toxic salt solution  for five days being poisoned and scalded  to what was intended to be my death and  on the fifth day of the abortion  procedure I was accidentally born alive  you know sadly there were demands made  to lead me to die at St Luke's Hospital  in Sioux City Iowa by my own grandmother  who was a nurse at that facility and  gratefully uh after a few minutes I know  that I was ultimately rushed off to the  NICU by a brave nurse who was willing to  do the right thing for me and for me  that's what the born alive vote is all  about is ensuring that babies like me  are provided Medical Care my life no  survivor's life should ever be left in  the hands of whoever is working that day  the short version of the bill would be  that it would  start the process where we would have  reporting of the incidence of failed  abortions and abortion survivors there  is no federal reporting that happens and  obviously we need to know just how big  of a problem this is in order to meet  the needs of survivors and women and  also medical providers that are impacted  by this so we're looking at reporting  we're looking at ensuring that babies  are provided Medical Care and not being  left to die people can look through CDC  reports and know that babies can survive  minutes hours days after failed  abortions without medical care  this should not ever be a question  uh it also would ensure that women who  experience a failed abortion could have  could take a stand right could sue the  abortionist if they don't provide their  child Medical Care knowing that it was  blocked over 80 times when we had  speaker Pelosi obviously yesterday was  very historic which is why it is  essential that this body the United  States House of Representatives condemns  these heinous acts of political violence  I am proud to be an original co-sponsor  of this legislation and will always and  forever stand on the right side of  history when it comes to protecting The  Unborn certainly it's so emotional to be  in that gallery and see the vote  happening  there were Democrats dressed all in  white making their stand that they of  course were standing in opposition to  the bill and it's almost Indescribable  for me to say what that's like to see  the people who are in opposition of  truly who I am and what I have suffered  and and the population that I serve what  they're suffering still today expecting  parents have enough worries they should  not have to worry about extreme  politicians in their doctor's office or  Hospital  thinking they somehow know better I urge  my colleagues to vote no on H.R 26. it  is a bit unnerving to see that but I've  been doing this for so long that it  doesn't surprise me but I I'm so so  emotional every time I see our leaders  our Republican leaders taking that stand  the messaging that has come out in the  last week is that the Republicans are  clearly taking a stand and sending a  message uh that that they're trying to  restrict abortion and for me what I look  upon what has happened I look at that  and say they are taking a stand in  defense of life and not just for  children like beef but for women like my  biological mother who deserved better  than to have an abortion forced upon her  but the same arguments we've heard for a  decade are the same arguments I heard  yesterday and I've seen it even today in  the media and none of it surprises me  but it's everything from this doesn't  happen well are they asking any of us  who have lived to tell this story what  our experiences are they asking these  moms are they looking at data the way  that we do what about all of these  instances and what about all of the  reports in the handful of States who  actually do report out their statistics  why is it that in States like Minnesota  and Texas when they identified babies  are surviving abortions you read in  those reports that those children were  not provided in medical care tell me  there isn't a problem  put themselves in the shoes of someone  like me who not only suffered trauma in  the womb but has suffered trauma  throughout my life as a result of it not  just emotional but physically the way  that abortion has affected my body I may  not be missing limbs but I can tell you  my body has been impacted by that  abortion ending my life  is not the solution to that problem  ensuring that that never happened in the  first place is what should have happened  and so I want people to really kind of  take a step back from all of the fight  that happens in social media in  particular and be willing to listen to  stories right be open-minded to the  other side of things and contact us ask  some ask some questions I would be more  than willing to have a conversation with  someone but there is more to the story  than what we have lived with for the  last 50 years under row
 

